RELATE finding:hud_bar_team_tint_confirm->cites->source:hud_font_tcw_setter;

-- ============================================================================
-- 36c (2026-06-14): ENGINE HUD QUAD SUBMIT/WINDING ORDER re-grounded end-to-end
-- (the authoritative basis for the client strip order) + the two prior claims
-- reconciled with explicit CONFIRMED/REFUTED, cross-cited to disasm + flycast TA
-- parser + a LIVE 143-quad HUDQ capture rendered through pvr2. feat/render-replica-live.
-- ============================================================================

UPSERT source:hud_engine_submit_order SET kind='code',
  ref='marvelous2 bank0f loc_8C0F6044-loc_8C0F6056 (HUD glyph poly record builder) -> hands record r13+0x34 to bank12.loc_8c1294C8 (cell processor) which emits the PVR TA strip; flycast TA parser core/hw/pvr/ta_vtx.cpp: ta_poly_data L370-406 (walks Vertex_Parameter list, EndOfStrip terminates), vert_cvt_base_ L709-721 (vd_rc.verts.emplace_back per vertex, SUBMIT ORDER, NO reorder), EndPolyStrip L687-698 (PolyParam.first/.count span the contiguous submit run); makeIndex core/hw/pvr/ta_util.cpp L450-524 (strip->triangle index build, parity-duplicate preserves v0,v1,v2,v3 order). collectHudQuads core/network/maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp:3055-3066 stores vidx[0..3] = first 4 submit-order verts.',
  note='THE ENGINE HUD VERTEX/CORNER SUBMIT ORDER, ground truth for the client re-tile. The MVC2 HUD polys are PVR para TYPE 4 (Polygon, ListType 0 Opaque), Textured, StripLen=3 (max 4 verts) — CONFIRMED by decoding the LIVE-captured pcw 0x808c00xx from the 143-quad HUDQ tail: ParaType(bits29-31)=4, ListType(24-26)=0, Texture(bit3)=1, StripLen(bits18-19)=3 (NOT a type-5 Sprite). The engine submits each HUD poly as a 4-vertex PVR TRIANGLE STRIP (v0,v1,v2,v3). flycast ta_vtx.cpp appends each strip vertex to vd_rc.verts in pure submit order (vert_cvt_base_ emplace_back, no permutation); EndPolyStrip records PolyParam.first/.count over that contiguous run. collectHudQuads captures vidx[0..3] = exactly those first 4 submit-order verts. The hardware strip rule for a 4-vert strip is the IDENTITY: verts (0,1,2,3) tessellate to triangles (0,1,2)+(1,2,3) with the shared diagonal between v1 and v2. THEREFORE the correct client re-tile is the IDENTITY strip [0,1,2,3] (the engine`s own two triangles), NOT a perimeter-walk [0,1,3,2]. This CONFIRMS the render-expert`s [0,1,2,3] fix. PROOF (live, rendered through the real pvr2 path, _hud_cap/names_zoom_{0123,0132}.png): [0,1,2,3] -> readable "TIME"/"LEVEL"/digits + clean bars; [0,1,3,2] -> diagonally mis-tiled glyph-slice noise == the exact live garble symptom. The corner coords confirm strips, not bbox: e.g. quad[1] x=[33,33,36,36] y=[67,49,69,46] is an angled italic parallelogram (top/bottom edges sheared), so a bbox or wrong-diagonal tiling shears every glyph.';

UPSERT finding:hud_engine_submit_winding_confirmed SET
  statement='ENGINE HUD QUAD SUBMIT/WINDING ORDER = a 4-vertex PVR triangle STRIP in native submit order (v0,v1,v2,v3) -> hardware triangles (0,1,2)+(1,2,3); the correct client re-tile is the IDENTITY strip [0,1,2,3]. GROUNDING: (1) PVR para type 4 Polygon / ListType 0 Opaque / StripLen 3 / Textured, decoded from the LIVE HUDQ pcw 0x808c00xx (143-quad capture, source:hudq_live_capture_2026_06_14) — NOT a type-5 Sprite, so it is a real strip whose corner order is meaningful. (2) flycast`s TA parser preserves submit order with ZERO reordering (ta_vtx.cpp vert_cvt_base_ emplace_back per vertex; EndPolyStrip spans PolyParam.first/.count over the contiguous run; makeIndex parity-duplication preserves v0..v3), so collectHudQuads vidx[0..3] (maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp:3055) ARE the engine`s own submit-order corners. (3) The bank0f HUD poly builder (loc_8C0F6044) hands the record to the bank12 cell processor (loc_8c1294C8) which emits that strip. (4) EMPIRICAL: rendering the captured corners as [0,1,2,3] through the real pvr2 path yields readable HUD; [0,1,3,2] yields the live garble (_hud_cap/names_zoom_*.png). So the engine order IS the identity strip and [0,1,2,3] is CONFIRMED correct. The captured corners are angled parallelograms (sheared italic glyphs), which is why the wrong diagonal ([0,1,3,2]) shears each glyph into colour-noise rather than just flipping a quad.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

UPSERT finding:hud_prior_detwiddle_claim_refuted SET
  statement='RECONCILE / RETRACTION of two prior conflicting claims. CLAIM A (a prior mvc2-sh4-re-expert run): "the pvr2 HUD path is not detwiddling RGB565 twiddled, so the client decodes the FONT texture wrong." THIS IS REFUTED. It was an INFERENCE about CLIENT code the prior run never read; the client DOES apply the Morton/PVR detwiddle for RGB565 twiddled (the render-expert verified texture-manager.mjs:172 `scan===0 ? <linear> : twop(x,y,bx,by)` — twop is the twiddle path, taken when ScanOrder==0). The font DECODE is correct: the SAME bytes from LIVE prod VRAM 0x4DF000 (TCW 0x0809BE00) decoded RGB565+detwiddle yield clean readable glyphs (source:hud_font_vram_dump, /dev/shm/mc_vram_dump.bin, re-confirmed 2026-06-14: twiddled=readable "0123456/LEVEL/TIME/MAX/WINS/LOSES"+gauge; linear=colour-noise). NOTE: an earlier note in THIS file (finding:hud_font_glyph_decode_truth) also leaned toward "client samples without the twiddle" as the root cause — that too is now SUPERSEDED by the strip-order finding; the twiddle decode was already correct client-side. CLAIM B (the real cause): "the garble is the TRIANGLE-STRIP CORNER ORDER in the client re-tile (buildHudTA defaulting to [0,1,3,2] instead of the engine`s identity strip [0,1,2,3])." THIS IS CONFIRMED — by the engine submit order being a native 4-vert strip (finding:hud_engine_submit_winding_confirmed) AND the live render proof that [0,1,2,3] reads clean while [0,1,3,2] garbles. ONE RECONCILED TRUTH: decode (format=RGB565, scan=twiddled, dims, palette, VRAM presence) is correct on BOTH engine and client; the garble was the strip-order re-tile, now fixed to the engine`s identity [0,1,2,3].',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

RELATE finding:hud_engine_submit_winding_confirmed->cites->source:hud_engine_submit_order;
RELATE finding:hud_engine_submit_winding_confirmed->cites->source:hudq_live_capture_2026_06_14;
RELATE finding:hud_engine_submit_winding_confirmed->cites->source:hud_render_routine_rom;
RELATE finding:hud_engine_submit_winding_confirmed->about->finding:hud_font_garble_strip_order;
RELATE finding:hud_prior_detwiddle_claim_refuted->cites->source:hud_font_vram_dump;
RELATE finding:hud_prior_detwiddle_claim_refuted->about->finding:hud_engine_submit_winding_confirmed;
RELATE finding:hud_prior_detwiddle_claim_refuted->about->finding:hud_font_glyph_decode_truth;

-- ============================================================================
-- 36d (2026-06-14): INDEPENDENT CLIENT-SIDE re-grounding by the render-pipeline
-- expert. The 36c grounding leaned on the C++ flycast TA parser (the SERVER-side
-- capture); this pins the CLIENT-side triangulation that ACTUALLY draws the
-- captured corners (pvr2-renderer.mjs), plus a fresh live pixel-diff. Closes the
-- chain end-to-end on the code the browser runs. feat/render-replica-live.
-- ============================================================================

UPSERT source:hud_client_retile_pvr2 SET kind='code',
  ref='web/webgpu/pvr2-renderer.mjs _buildIndexBuffer (grep the name; was ~L142-164); web/render-replica/replay.html buildHudTA (grep; was ~L571-619, order default [0,1,2,3] @ the `order =` line); core/network/maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp collectHudQuads (grep; storage loop ~L3055-3066); core/hw/pvr/ta_vtx.cpp vert_cvt_base_ (emplace_back per vertex) + glob_param_bdc_ (d_pp->first = verts.size()) + EndPolyStrip (count = verts.size()-first); web/webgpu/texture-manager.mjs _decode (idx = scan===1 ? linear : twop(...)).',
  note='THE CLIENT DRAW PATH, ground-truthed on the code the BROWSER runs (the 36c grounding cited the C++ parser; this is the JS that re-tiles the captured corners). CHAIN, each link cited: (1) CAPTURE STORES SUBMIT ORDER — collectHudQuads walks k=pp.first..pp.first+pp.count over rc.idx[k] (or rc.verts directly for autosort tr), takes the first 4 into vidx[nv++], then copies vidx[c] straight into q.x[c]/y[c]/u[c]/v[c]/col[c] with NO reorder; the C++ verts were appended in pure TA submit order (ta_vtx.cpp vert_cvt_base_ emplace_back; pp.first/.count span that contiguous run). => q.x[0..3] ARE engine strip verts V0,V1,V2,V3. (2) CLIENT RE-TILES AS A STRIP IN ARRAY ORDER — pvr2-renderer.mjs _buildIndexBuffer triangulates a count-vertex PolyParam as a GPU triangle strip from pp.first: for i in 0..count-2, even i -> (v0,v1,v2), odd i -> (v1,v0,v2) [winding-flip]; for count=4 this is triangles (V0,V1,V2)+(V2,V1,V3) == the hardware strip (0,1,2)+(1,2,3). It consumes the 4 verts in the ORDER THEY SIT IN THE ARRAY. (3) buildHudTA writes the 4 corners into that array in order[k] sequence; identity order=[0,1,2,3] feeds V0,V1,V2,V3 back in their captured submit order => reproduces the engine`s OWN two triangles byte-for-byte. order=[0,1,3,2] swaps V2<->V3 => strip triangles (0,1,3)+(3,1,2), a bowtie/wrong-diagonal mis-tile of each sheared italic glyph slice = the garble. (4) DECODE IS CORRECT — texture-manager.mjs _decode: `const idx = scan===1 ? y*w+x : twop(x,y,bx,by)`; FONT tcw 0x0809BE00 has ScanOrder bit26=0 => twop (Morton detwiddle) IS applied; fmt=1 => u565 RGB565. CONFIRMED by reading the exact line. So [0,1,2,3] is PROVEN from source (capture-order + client strip triangulation + identity re-tile), independent of "it looked readable".';

UPSERT source:hud_pixel_diff_2026_06_14 SET kind='oracle',
  ref='node tools/render-replica-poc/hudq_capture.mjs --url wss://nobd.net/replica-live --frames 400 --want-hud 30 (saved _hud_cap_def/{vram_prefix.bin 8MB, pvr_prefix.bin 32KB, hudq_tail.bin 104 quads}); rendered via tools/render-replica-poc/render_hudq.mjs (Dawn/webgpu, pvr2-renderer+texture-manager+ta-parser VERBATIM) at --order 0,1,2,3 vs 0,1,3,2; FONT atlas ground-truthed via tools/render-replica-poc/_decode_font2.mjs (TextureManager._decode, fmt=1 RGB565 scan=0, VRAM 0x4DF000, 256x128).',
  note='FRESH LIVE PIXEL-DIFF PROOF (render-pipeline expert, independent of the 36c capture). Live capture: 104 HUD quads/frame. FONT GROUND TRUTH: _decode_font2.mjs decoded VRAM 0x4DF000 via the REAL client TextureManager._decode (RGB565, scan=0 twiddled) -> font_atlas_gt.png shows CLEAN readable glyph atlas ("TIME" yellow, "SENTINEL"/"LEVEL"/"MAX"/digit grids, the circular meter gauge), glyphs stored mirror-imaged (the FONT quads carry mirrored UVs u 0.996->0.754 to flip them upright) -> a non-detwiddled decode would be Morton-noise, so the decode/twiddle is CONFIRMED correct. RENDER DIFF (P1bigname.png / P2bigname.png, top=[0,1,2,3] FIX, bottom=[0,1,3,2] OLD): FIX -> clean upright white glyphs ("NEL" tail of SENTINEL, "BLE" tail of CABLE) + clean red/yellow meter bars; OLD -> same glyph rows sheared + the meter bars show a DIAGONAL colour wedge/gradient-bleed (the bar quad`s two triangles tiled across the wrong diagonal, dragging the gouraud corner-to-corner) == the live garble symptom. NOTE on what the FONT.BIN 0x4DF000 region actually carries: the tcw=0x0809BE00 HUD quads are the angled FRAME/underline STROKES of the name plates (w=225 h=2, w=3 h=23 parallelograms with sheared corners e.g. y=[67,49,69,46]); the per-CHARACTER big-name letters are the fmt=5 PAL4 quads in the 0x445000+ bank (one tcw per glyph). BOTH families are 4-vert strips and BOTH are fixed by the identity re-tile. The control word confirms a real strip: live pcw 0x808c003e decodes ParaType=4 (Polygon), ListType=0 (Opaque), StripLen=3 (4 verts/2 tris), Texture=1, Gouraud=1 -> NOT a type-5 Sprite, so corner order is load-bearing.';

UPSERT finding:hud_garble_one_truth_clientgrounded SET
  statement='ONE GROUNDED TRUTH (render-pipeline expert, client-code-cited, pixel-proven). The HUD FONT/name garble was the CLIENT TRIANGLE-STRIP RE-TILE ORDER, NOT the texture decode. PROOF CHAIN (every link a read source line): (a) collectHudQuads stores the 4 corners in engine TA SUBMIT order with no reorder (oracle_hook.cpp collectHudQuads, vidx[c]->q.x[c]); (b) those C++ verts were appended in submit order (ta_vtx.cpp vert_cvt_base_ emplace_back; first/count span the run); (c) the CLIENT pvr2-renderer.mjs _buildIndexBuffer triangulates a PolyParam as a strip over pp.first..first+count IN ARRAY ORDER (even i->(v0,v1,v2), odd i->(v1,v0,v2)); (d) buildHudTA (replay.html) writes corners in order[k]; identity [0,1,2,3] => reproduces the engine strip (0,1,2)+(1,2,3); [0,1,3,2] => wrong diagonal => garble; (e) the live pcw 0x808c003e is ParaType=4/StripLen=3 (a real 4-vert strip, NOT a sprite) so the order matters; (f) DECODE is correct — texture-manager.mjs _decode applies twop (detwiddle) for scan=0, and the live VRAM 0x4DF000 decoded via the real TextureManager._decode yields clean glyphs (font_atlas_gt.png). PIXEL DIFF (source:hud_pixel_diff_2026_06_14): [0,1,2,3] clean / [0,1,3,2] diagonal-sheared bars+glyphs. RECONCILIATION (explicit): CLAIM "RGB565 not detwiddled" = REFUTED (texture-manager.mjs _decode line `scan===1 ? y*w+x : twop(x,y,bx,by)` applies the detwiddle for the FONT scan=0; glyphs decode clean). CLAIM "wrong triangle-strip order [0,1,3,2]->[0,1,2,3]" = CONFIRMED (capture-order + client strip triangulation + the live pixel diff). The fix is ALREADY deployed in replay.html buildHudTA (commit 52892ced1, order default [0,1,2,3]); this finding RE-GROUNDS that justification on the client code + a fresh live diff, replacing the earlier "engine native submit order" assertion with the cited capture->triangulate->retile chain. NO residual client bug remains for the strip path: [0,1,2,3] is correct for ALL HUD strips (FONT-frame, PAL4 glyphs, bars). Independent open items (NOT the garble, tracked elsewhere): the fmt=5 PAL4 meter art VRAM coverage (finding:hud_meter_segments_vram_gap) is a SERVER prefix gap; multi-glyph tier-2 name plates are a fidelity refinement.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

RELATE finding:hud_garble_one_truth_clientgrounded->cites->source:hud_client_retile_pvr2;
RELATE finding:hud_garble_one_truth_clientgrounded->cites->source:hud_pixel_diff_2026_06_14;
RELATE finding:hud_garble_one_truth_clientgrounded->about->finding:hud_engine_submit_winding_confirmed;
RELATE finding:hud_garble_one_truth_clientgrounded->about->finding:hud_prior_detwiddle_claim_refuted;
RELATE finding:hud_garble_one_truth_clientgrounded->about->finding:hud_font_garble_strip_order;
